            "section": "QA",
            "category": "Arithmetic",
            "questionType": "TITA",
            "questionText": "A trader sells a product at a 20% discount on the marked price and still makes a profit of 25%. If the cost price is $400, what is the marked price ($)?",
            "correctAnswer": "625",
            "acceptedAnswers": [
              "625",
              "625.0"
            ],
            "explanation": "Selling Price = 400 * 1.25 = $500. Marked Price * (1 - 0.20) = 500 => MP * 0.8 = 500 => MP = 500 / 0.8 = $625.",
