            "passageTitle": "Reading Comprehension 3: Algorithmic Governance",
            "passageText": "The integration of algorithmic decision-making systems into automated judicial and financial administration introduces novel challenges for accountability. Because machine learning models function as opaque black boxes, auditing decision-making criteria becomes exceptionally difficult. Legal scholars advocate for explainable AI frameworks that guarantee transparency without compromising proprietary algorithms.",
